<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Strait of Otranto</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Strait of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otranto">Otranto</a> connects the Adriatic Sea with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a>, separating the heel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> at Otranto from Albania. About 72 kilometres wide, it has long been a crossing point between Italy and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> and a strategic choke point; in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> blockaded it with the Otranto Barrage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/strait-of-otranto.jpg" alt="Strait of Otranto" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vagabond nanoda · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strait_of_Otranto_closeup.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
